    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOI7W0xc7DW-Cd",
      "title": "Fix CircleCI BQ auth: prefer OIDC v1 token over v2",
      "author": "MSilb7",
      "number": 1793,
      "body": "## Summary\n- Fixes daily CI/CD BQ authentication failure caused by `google.subject exceeds 127 bytes` error\n- The `refresh_oidc_token_file()` function was preferring `CIRCLE_OIDC_TOKEN_V2`, whose `sub` claim includes VCS info (full repo URL + branch name), exceeding GCP Workload Identity Federation's 127-byte `google.subject` limit\n- Swapped preference to use `CIRCLE_OIDC_TOKEN` (v1) first, which has the shorter subject format (`org/<uuid>/project/<uuid>/user/<uuid>`)\n\n## Test plan\n- [ ] Trigger the `daily_l2_chain_data_uploads` CI job and verify BQ writes succeed without the 127-byte auth error\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/op-analytics",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-12T18:31:35Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-02-12T18:33:43Z",
      "additions": 234,
      "deletions": 167
    },
